# Eden SX2A Guardrails

- Before new work, read `brain/CHECKPOINT.md`, `brain/CURRENT_STATE.md`, `brain/NEXT_ACTIONS.md`.
- Evidence labels only: VERIFIED | PARTIALLY_VERIFIED | IMPLEMENTED_NOT_TESTED | HYPOTHESIS | BLOCKED | NOT_STARTED.
- Do not declare compatibility or performance wins without measurements.
- Prefer subsystem fixes over per-title hacks; isolate temporary workarounds.
- Publish only to fork remote `origin` on `sx2a/*`. Never push to `upstream`. Never open upstream PRs unless the owner explicitly asks.
- Never force-push; keep `baseline/59bb148` and tag `baseline-m0-59bb148` intact.
- Public fork: no games, keys, firmware, secrets, PII, sensitive logs, or unnecessary local machine config in git. Follow `brain/STORAGE_POLICY.md` and `brain/GIT_WORKFLOW.md`.
- Do not disable thermal protections or use root/overclock to pass tests.
- Android diagnostic package: `dev.eden.nx2.relWithDebInfo`.
- Memory work must distinguish guest VA / DRAM layout / host RSS; 12GB layout intends 12GiB+8GiB DRAM (`k_system_control.*`).
- Follow `brain/GUARDRAILS.md` and upstream `docs/policies/AI.md` / `AGENTS.md` for upstream-bound contributions.
